### Bug Description

Following up on issue #11702 , after in-depth research and analyzing the logs with the help of AI, I found that the reason MinerU-MCP service failed to start properly is that Cherry Studio lacks administrator privileges to create directories, so it cannot be enabled, as shown in the image below. (In addition, the issue where log content in black boxes is still not visible in light mode has not been fixed; see #11887 for details.)

<img width="1052" height="969" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/71c00e4b-5df4-4b43-940c-a9d245186525" />

Therefore, is it possible to display a popup reminding the user that administrator privileges are required when a problem caused by a lack of administrator privileges is detected, or to automatically pop up a UAC prompt after the first installation failure?

In addition, I noticed that since the log function was enabled, the MCP server frequently displays black triangle question mark boxes. I am not sure what this is, and checking the application's general logs did not reveal anything, as shown in the image below.

<img width="1111" height="1058" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2322c815-b76a-48aa-8722-ee104fcc2df2" />

